# AGENTS.md

Instructions for coding agents working on {{ title }}, a Navree microservice
from the `{{ kit }}` starter kit: a Rust service that answers messages and
handles events over a broker (NATS), with modules wired by dependency
injection. Read this file before changing code.

## Layout

```text
Cargo.toml                         the workspace; its default member is the service
config/app.toml                    settings shared by every environment (committed)
.env                               this machine's secrets and Dock's settings (never committed)
dock.toml                          local services: `navree dock up` (PostgreSQL, NATS)
harbor.toml                        servers and deploys: `navree deploy`
crates/{{ contracts_package }}/    the messages and events, shared with the services that call this one
crates/{{ package }}/src/main.rs   runs the service: `serve` by default, or any other command
crates/{{ package }}/src/app.rs    the root: the framework modules, MicroModule, the feature modules
crates/{{ package }}/src/modules/  feature modules: invoices
crates/{{ package }}/tests/        tests that boot the service on MicroFake, without a broker
```

## Commands

Run them at the workspace root (`cargo run` runs the service there):

```sh
navree dock up                                          # {{ database_name }} and NATS in containers
navree dev                                              # handlers on NATS, health on :8080, rebuild on save
cargo test --workspace                                  # every test; no broker needed
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings   # must pass
cargo fmt                                               # must leave nothing to change
navree check                                            # validate the module graph without booting
navree micro:patterns                                   # every message and event pattern with its access rule
navree micro:send invoices.get '{"id":"..."}'           # send a message and print the reply
navree micro:failed                                     # dead-lettered events (`micro:retry <id|all>`)
navree migrate                                          # run pending migrations
```

`cargo fmt` formats the workspace's crates; `--all` would also format path
dependencies. The generators (`navree make:module`, `make:migration`, ...) work on one
package: run them in `crates/{{ package }}`.

## Messages and events

- **The contract comes first.** A new message or event starts as a type in
  `crates/{{ contracts_package }}`: the payload (`Serialize`, `Deserialize`,
  `garde::Validate`), the reply type, and a pattern constant
  (`invoices.get`) or an `impl Event` whose `NAME` is the pattern
  (`deal.won`). Services that call this one depend on the crate, so a
  changed payload is a compile error on both sides.
- **Handlers** are methods of an `#[injectable]` struct with a
  `#[message_handlers]` impl block, registered in the module's `wire` with
  `m.message_handlers::<T>()`. Copy `src/modules/invoices/handlers.rs`:
  `#[message_pattern("x.y")]` answers `ServiceClient::send`,
  `#[event_pattern("x.y")]` handles what `ServiceClient::emit` publishes.
- **Deny by default.** A message pattern declares who may call it:
  `#[public]`, `#[authenticated]`, `#[roles(..)]`, `#[permissions(..)]` or
  `#[can(Action, Subject, from = "id")]`. The caller's bearer token travels
  with the message and is verified with `auth.jwt.secret`, the same in
  every service. Event patterns take no access declaration.
- **Input.** Take `Valid(Payload(input)): Valid<Payload<T>>`; an invalid
  message is a 400 reply, an invalid event goes straight to the dead
  letters.
- **Unit of work.** Take `uow: Uow` and pass `&uow` to services; it commits
  when the handler returns `Ok`. Events emitted with `ServiceClient::emit`
  inside it are published after the commit (the outbox), never for work
  that rolled back.
- **Idempotency.** An event can arrive more than once (the inbox skips a
  repeated message id, not a repeated fact): make handlers safe to run
  again, as `draft_for_deal` is with its one-invoice-per-deal rule.
- **Errors.** Handlers return `Result<T>` (`AppError`): the caller gets the
  same `{ "statusCode", "message", "error", "code" }` error as over HTTP.

## Conventions

- **Database.** SeaORM entities with UUID v7 ids; writes take the unit of
  work first and go through `Repo` (audited). Migrations belong to their
  module's `MigrationSet`; never edit one that has run anywhere, add a new
  one.
- **Configuration.** `config/app.toml` holds shared settings; secrets go in
  `.env` or the environment (`APP_AUTH__JWT__SECRET`). Another broker:
  change `micro.transport` and the `micro-*` feature in
  `crates/{{ package }}/Cargo.toml` together; the handlers don't change.
- **Tests.** Every change comes with tests. `tests/support/mod.rs` boots
  the service with the committed `config/app.toml` on a fresh SQLite
  database and `MicroFake`'s in-memory transport: send messages with
  `micro.client().send(..)`, deliver events with `micro.client().emit(..)`,
  and assert on what the service emitted with `micro.assert_emitted(..)`.

## Before you finish

Run `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`
and `cargo test --workspace`, and fix everything they report.

